# Formation DS — Documentation First

IMPORTANT: This is a non-negotiable rule. Never assume component structure, token values, or design patterns. Always read the source of truth first.

## Before any Formation-related work

1. Read the relevant documentation in `.agents/skills/formation-design-system/references/core/`:
   - `components.md` — component catalog, HTML structure, token specs
   - `colors.md` — color tokens and semantic aliases
   - `typography.md` — type scale, font families, weights
   - `spacing.md` — spacing scale
   - `radius.md` — border-radius tokens
2. For business-unit theming, also read `.agents/skills/formation-design-system/references/business-units/*.md`
3. When implementing UI from Figma or making canvas edits, use the **local** Figma Console MCP (`figmaConsoleMcpLocal`) — this runs via `npx figma-console-mcp` on localhost and connects to the Desktop Bridge plugin over WebSocket. The remote southleft.com upstream is blocked by org policy.
   - To read/inspect: call `figma_execute` with a read-only script returning node data
   - To write/edit: call `figma_execute` with a mutating script
   - Do NOT use `figma_get_file_data` or any tool that targets `https://figma-console-mcp.southleft.com/mcp` — these are policy-blocked
4. Figma Core Components file key: `prQIPGE33uoH1SyxfVTFKT`

## What is forbidden

- IMPORTANT: Never invent token values, rgba workarounds, or approximate component structures
- IMPORTANT: Never hardcode colors, spacing, or radii — always use Formation tokens
- Never assume a component's HTML structure — read `components.md` or query Figma first
- Never create light/dark mode variants of tokens that do not exist in Formation

## Available skills (use them)

- `formation-design-system` — look up any token, component spec, or theme value
- `validate-formation-usage` — audit code or Figma for Formation compliance
- `create-figma-plugin` — scaffold a new Figma plugin with Formation styling
- `integrate-knowledge-base` — onboard a project to Formation (sets up .cursorrules)
- `refresh-formation-tokens` — regenerate Formation docs after a package version bump
